    "title": "pandas.Series.dt.start_time — pandas 2.0.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.dt.start_time#\n\n- Series.dt.start_time[source]#\n- Get the Timestamp for the start of the period. \n  - Returns\n    - Timestamp\n See also \n  - `Period.end_time`\n  - Return the end Timestamp.\n  - `Period.dayofyear`\n  - Return the day of year.\n  - `Period.daysinmonth`\n  - Return the days in that month.\n  - `Period.dayofweek`\n  - Return the day of the week.\n Examples >>> period = pd.Period('2012-1-1', freq='D') >>> period Period('2012-01-01', 'D') >>> period.start_time Timestamp('2012-01-01 00:00:00') >>> period.end_time Timestamp('2012-01-01 23:59:59.999999999')",
    "markdown_length": 580,
